    {
      "turn": 1,
      "doctor_question": "Hello, I'm Dr. Smith. It's nice to meet you. Could you please tell me what brings you in to see me today?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S003",
      "patient_response": "Hey Dr. Smith. Nice to meet you too. Uh, well, what brought me in is... basically, people keep getting on my case, saying I’m not listening to them. \n\nLike my supervisor at the plant, or my wife. They'll be talking straight to me, right? Just looking right at me. And... well, speaking of my supervisor, he was just on my back yesterday about the new stamping press. We got this new machine on the production floor and it's supposed to be faster, but it keeps jamming on the quarter-inch plates. I told him the alignment was off, but he wouldn't hear it. The maintenance guy, Frank, he's a good guy, but he's been out sick with some kind of flu, so the whole line is just a mess right now. \n\nAnyway, what was I saying? Oh, right, listening. Yeah, so my supervisor or my wife will be talking right to my face, and a minute later I realize I only caught maybe half of what they said. So I have to ask them to say it all over again, and man, they get so mad. Especially my wife, like if she's talking about her sister's new dog or something. Have you ever had a Golden Retriever? They shed like crazy, it gets all over the couch. But yeah, that's why I'm here, I guess. The listening thing.",
